<title>USA: NAIC downgrades TCI debt-NAIC official.</title>
<headline>NAIC downgrades TCI debt-NAIC official.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Association of Insurance Commissioners (NAIC) said it downgraded TCI Communications Inc debt to an NAIC-three from an NAIC-two rating on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Earlier, market players cited spreads on TCI debt widen by 20 basis points on rumors of the NAIC rating action. Other cable-sector bonds have widened in sympathy, traders said.</p>
<p>The NAIC official declined further comment.</p>
<p>-U.S. Corporate Bond Desk, 212-859-1662</p>
</text>
